<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentView xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="CardiTrack.Mobile.Controls.QuickActionRow">

    <!-- The three ways to reach a CardiMember, lifted out of DashboardPage so the alert detail
         screen offers the same three rather than a second, differently-worded set of its own.

         Quick actions (issue #162): Call and Message reach the CardiMember's own phone directly.
         SOS is visually distinct (tinted, not a plain white tile) precisely because it dials
         someone else, not the member this row is about — its label dropped the member's name
         (issue: names vary in length once more than one CardiMember can appear). Each tile dims
         independently when its own number is missing (issue #67's dim-not-hide pattern) — they
         stay tappable so the tap can explain why, the only affordance a dimmed tile has on touch.
         SOS leads the row: it is the one action with a deadline on it, and the first tile is where
         a thumb lands and where the eye starts. The others are reachable in the seconds that
         emergency is not.

         Details was the fourth tile until 2026-09-26. It opened Member Details, which a tap on
         the dashboard card already does and Alert Details reaches through its own "activity data"
         link, so the tile was a second door to one room — and the space it held on the dashboard
         card's foot now carries the card's news (see MemberDashboardCard).

         Each tile is a transparent cell carrying the tap, the tooltip and the accessible name,
         with the tinted face drawn inside it and deaf to touch. In the full row the cell is
         simply the face's column; compact, it is a 48 square round a smaller face, so an
         icon-only tile is still a finger's width to hit (ApplyLayout).

         No inset round the grid. The tiles used to cast a shadow, and the row carried a gutter
         the shadow's size (with a matching negative margin at every call site) so Android would
         not clip it; they are raised by a gradient fill now (QuickActionTintBrush), so the grid
         fills the view and the call sites need no margin. -->

    <Grid x:Name="Tiles" ColumnDefinitions="*,*,*" ColumnSpacing="10">
        <Grid x:Name="EmergencyCallAction"
              Grid.Column="0"
              BackgroundColor="Transparent"
              SemanticProperties.Description="SOS: call emergency contact"
              SemanticProperties.Hint="Dials the emergency contact number, not the CardiMember directly">
            <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="OnEmergencyCallTapped"/>
            </Grid.GestureRecognizers>
            <Border x:Name="SosTile"
                    Style="{StaticResource QuickActionTile}"
                    Background="{StaticResource QuickActionTintRedBrush}"
                    InputTransparent="True">
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">
                    <!-- The same handset as Call, in the destructive red rather than the
                         brand blue: this tile dials the emergency contact, and it was the
                         only thing on it still saying "ordinary call" while the tint and
                         the label both said otherwise. DangerRed clears 3:1 on the red
                         tint (3.97) where the label's StatusRed does not (2.96). -->
                    <Image x:Name="SosIcon"
                           Source="icon_action_sos.svg"
                           WidthRequest="22" HeightRequest="22"
                           HorizontalOptions="Center"/>
                    <Label x:Name="SosLabel"
                           Text="SOS"
                           Style="{StaticResource QuickActionLabel}"
                           TextColor="{StaticResource StatusRed}"
                           LineBreakMode="TailTruncation"/>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>
        </Grid>
        <Grid x:Name="CallAction"
              Grid.Column="1"
              BackgroundColor="Transparent"
              SemanticProperties.Description="Call">
            <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="OnCallTapped"/>
            </Grid.GestureRecognizers>
            <Border x:Name="CallTile"
                    Style="{StaticResource QuickActionTile}"
                    Background="{StaticResource QuickActionTintBrush}"
                    InputTransparent="True">
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">
                    <Image x:Name="CallIcon"
                           Source="icon_action_call.svg"
                           WidthRequest="22" HeightRequest="22"
                           HorizontalOptions="Center"/>
                    <Label x:Name="CallLabel"
                           Text="Call"
                           Style="{StaticResource QuickActionLabel}"
                           LineBreakMode="TailTruncation"/>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>
        </Grid>
        <Grid x:Name="MessageAction"
              Grid.Column="2"
              BackgroundColor="Transparent"
              SemanticProperties.Description="Message">
            <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="OnMessageTapped"/>
            </Grid.GestureRecognizers>
            <Border x:Name="MessageTile"
                    Style="{StaticResource QuickActionTile}"
                    Background="{StaticResource QuickActionTintBrush}"
                    InputTransparent="True">
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">
                    <Image x:Name="MessageIcon"
                           Source="icon_action_sms.svg"
                           WidthRequest="22" HeightRequest="22"
                           HorizontalOptions="Center"/>
                    <Label x:Name="MessageLabel" Text="Message" Style="{StaticResource QuickActionLabel}"/>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</ContentView>
